<title>FRANCE: Total seen raising dividend.</title>
<headline>Total seen raising dividend.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>French energy group Total SA could increase its 1996 dividend, and a level of 10 francs per share, from 8.70 francs in 1995, is possible, chairman Thierry Desmarest told the Journal des Finances.</p>
<p>Asked whether the dividend would be raised to 10 francs per share, he said: &quot;It is certainly a possibility but it is far too soon to announce a precise figure today.&quot;</p>
<p>He added there was a debate in the company whether it would continue giving a share alternative for the dividend payment.</p>
</text>
